From 2a730081f5b3e3f92d966a34a13ce1cecd1ad783 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NikoMalik <NikoMalik@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 02:55:05 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] sched/poc: skip the pending RMW when the bit is already set

__set_cpu_idle_state_poc() runs on every idle entry and exit of every CPU
and did a locked atomic_or() on the per-LLC pending word each time,pulling
that shared line exclusive,in a game it was about 1% of kernel cycles

if this CPU's bit is still pending the aggregator has not consumed it and
re-reads poc_busy_bit after its atomic_xchg(),so read the word first and
skip the RMW,an smp_mb() orders the poc_busy_bit store before that read
and pairs with the full barrier of the xchg
---
 kernel/sched/poc_selector.c | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/kernel/sched/poc_selector.c b/kernel/sched/poc_selector.c
index f34e9c75a2b9..ac05c60a0f6e 100644
--- a/kernel/sched/poc_selector.c
+++ b/kernel/sched/poc_selector.c
@@ -675,6 +675,17 @@ void __set_cpu_idle_state_poc(int cpu, int state)
 	 */
 	if (!!((u64)atomic64_read(&sd_share->poc_busy_mask) & bm) == !state)
 		return;
+	/*
+	 * Every CPU of the LLC enters and leaves idle through here and the
+	 * locked RMW pulls the shared pending line exclusive each time. If
+	 * this CPU's bit is still pending the aggregator has not consumed it
+	 * yet and re-reads poc_busy_bit after its atomic_xchg(), so a plain
+	 * read is enough. The barrier orders the poc_busy_bit store before
+	 * that read, pairing with the full barrier of the xchg.
+	 */
+	smp_mb();
+	if (atomic_read(&sd_share->poc_pending[bit >> 3]) & (1 << (bit & 7)))
+		return;
 	atomic_or(1 << (bit & 7), &sd_share->poc_pending[bit >> 3]);
 }
 /**************************************************************
